---
layout: layouts/base.njk
---
<section class="hero">
  <div class="hero__inner">
    <div class="hero__copy">
      <span class="hero__eyebrow"><span class="dot"></span> Field-tested · NIMS · FEMA · OGC</span>
      <h1>Python for emergency response &amp; <span class="accent">incident GIS</span> workflows.</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        A production-focused, field-tested technical resource for building reliable, compliant,
        and scalable Python GIS workflows tailored to emergency management. Every pattern is
        designed to work in the field — not just in a lab.
      </p>
      <p>
        Built for emergency management tech teams, GIS analysts, public safety developers, and
        government platform engineers, this site documents architecture patterns that prioritize
        operational continuity under intermittent connectivity, strict compliance mandates, and
        high-stakes decision timelines.
      </p>
      <p>
        Focus areas: incident location mapping, evacuation routing, shelter capacity tracking,
        real-time multi-agency sync, alert automation, reporting, and failover planning.
      </p>

      <div class="hero__cta">
        {% for section in site.sections %}
          <a class="cta {% if loop.first %}cta--primary{% elif loop.index0 == 1 %}cta--ember{% else %}cta--rose{% endif %}" href="{{ site.url }}/{{ section.slug }}/">
            <span class="cta__icon">
              {% include "partials/icon-" + section.icon + ".njk" ignore missing %}
            </span>
            <span>{{ section.short }}</span>
          </a>
        {% endfor %}
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="hero__art" aria-hidden="true">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 420 420" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
        <defs>
          <radialGradient id="halo" cx="50%" cy="50%" r="60%">
            <stop offset="0%" stop-color="#ffb199" stop-opacity="0.9"/>
            <stop offset="55%" stop-color="#ff5a5f" stop-opacity="0.5"/>
            <stop offset="100%" stop-color="#7a0a1f" stop-opacity="0"/>
          </radialGradient>
          <linearGradient id="pin3" x1="0%" y1="0%" x2="0%" y2="100%">
            <stop offset="0%" stop-color="#ff3b5c"/>
            <stop offset="60%" stop-color="#c8102e"/>
            <stop offset="100%" stop-color="#7a0a1f"/>
          </linearGradient>
          <linearGradient id="ringg" x1="0%" y1="0%" x2="100%" y2="100%">
            <stop offset="0%" stop-color="#ffd1d8"/>
            <stop offset="100%" stop-color="#ff6b6b"/>
          </linearGradient>
        </defs>
        <circle cx="210" cy="220" r="200" fill="url(#halo)"/>
        <circle cx="210" cy="220" r="148" fill="none" stroke="url(#ringg)" stroke-width="3" stroke-dasharray="2 8" opacity="0.7"/>
        <circle cx="210" cy="220" r="118" fill="none" stroke="#ff6b6b" stroke-width="2" stroke-dasharray="4 6" opacity="0.6"/>
        <circle cx="210" cy="220" r="88"  fill="none" stroke="#c8102e" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-dasharray="6 8" opacity="0.55"/>
        <g stroke="#1a0008" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" opacity="0.4">
          <line x1="210" y1="40" x2="210" y2="58"/>
          <line x1="210" y1="382" x2="210" y2="400"/>
          <line x1="20" y1="220" x2="38" y2="220"/>
          <line x1="382" y1="220" x2="400" y2="220"/>
        </g>
        <!-- secondary pins -->
        <g opacity="0.85">
          <circle cx="120" cy="160" r="9" fill="#ffba2a"/>
          <circle cx="120" cy="160" r="4" fill="#7a0a1f"/>
          <circle cx="305" cy="120" r="8" fill="#ff5a3c"/>
          <circle cx="305" cy="120" r="3.5" fill="#7a0a1f"/>
          <circle cx="320" cy="300" r="9" fill="#c8102e"/>
          <circle cx="320" cy="300" r="4" fill="#fff5f5"/>
          <circle cx="100" cy="305" r="8" fill="#ff6b6b"/>
          <circle cx="100" cy="305" r="3.5" fill="#fff5f5"/>
        </g>
        <!-- main pin -->
        <path d="M210 80c-32 0-58 25-58 55.7 0 41 58 104.3 58 104.3s58-63.3 58-104.3C268 105 242 80 210 80z"
              fill="url(#pin3)" stroke="#1a0008" stroke-width="2"/>
        <circle cx="210" cy="138" r="20" fill="#fff5f5"/>
        <circle cx="210" cy="138" r="10" fill="#c8102e"/>
        <!-- sparks -->
        <path d="M320 60 L334 36 L330 70 L364 60 L334 78 L348 100 L320 84 L302 108 L308 80 L278 80 L308 70 Z"
              fill="#ffba2a" opacity="0.85"/>
      </svg>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section-shell">
  <div class="section-grid">
    {% for section in site.sections %}
      <a class="section-card section-card--{{ section.accent }}" href="{{ site.url }}/{{ section.slug }}/">
        <span class="section-card__icon">
          {% include "partials/icon-" + section.icon + ".njk" ignore missing %}
        </span>
        <h2>{{ section.title }}</h2>
        <p>{{ section.summary }}</p>
        <span class="section-card__more">Explore the section</span>
      </a>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section-shell">
  <div class="prose-shell">
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>What you'll find inside</h2>
      <p>
        Each section is organized into focused, deeply-linked technical guides covering the full
        lifecycle of emergency GIS — from coordinate reference system choice and field data
        ingestion through real-time multi-agency sync and reproducible Python toolchains. Alongside
        the core references you'll find head-to-head technology comparisons (FlatGeobuf vs GeoPackage,
        Kafka vs RabbitMQ), throughput benchmarks under simulated surge load, evacuation routing and
        shelter-capacity schemas, and consolidated NIMS, FEMA, and OGC compliance checklists. Every
        article includes working code, deterministic patterns, and schema definitions written for
        engineers shipping mission-critical systems in the field.
      </p>

      <ul>
        {% for section in site.sections %}
          {% set node = false %}
          {% for n in contentTree %}{% if n.slug == section.slug %}{% set node = n %}{% endif %}{% endfor %}
          {% if node %}
            <li>
              <strong><a href="{{ site.url }}{{ node.url }}">{{ section.title }}</a></strong> —
              {{ section.summary }}
              {% if node.children.length %}
                <ul>
                  {% for child in node.children %}
                    <li><a href="{{ site.url }}{{ child.url }}">{{ child.title }}</a>
                      {% if child.children and child.children.length %}
                        <ul>
                          {% for leaf in child.children %}
                            <li><a href="{{ site.url }}{{ leaf.url }}">{{ leaf.title }}</a></li>
                          {% endfor %}
                        </ul>
                      {% endif %}
                    </li>
                  {% endfor %}
                </ul>
              {% endif %}
            </li>
          {% endif %}
        {% endfor %}
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

